# Shell scripts are authored on Windows but run on Linux. Without this they can
# arrive with CRLF and fail as `$'\r': command not found`, which reads as a
# syntax error in the script rather than a line-ending problem.
*.sh text eol=lf
# sqlx records a SHA-384 of each migration's bytes and refuses to start if it
# changes. Checked out with CRLF on Windows and LF on a Linux CI runner, the
# same file hashes differently — an image built here and an image built in CI
# disagree, and the second one panics with VersionMismatch. Pin them to LF.
*.sql text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
